2Sa 3:1 , During the war David still waxes stronger;
2Sa 3:2 , Six sons are born to him in Hebron;
2Sa 3:6 , Abner, displeased with Ish-bosheth
2Sa 3:7 , revolts to David;
2Sa 3:13 , David requires as a condition to bring him his wife Michal;
2Sa 3:17 , Abner, having communed with the Israelites, is feasted by David, and dismissed;
2Sa 3:22 , Joab returning from battle, is displeased with the king, and kills Abner;
2Sa 3:28 , David curses Joab;
2Sa 3:31 , and mourns for Abner.
